now:
  companion_hashes: C59 propagates cancellation through all five preparation and every chunk hash. All 367 affected Node checks (93.43% line coverage) and nine Edge tests pass. Real OPFS fixtures retain the prior pointer, clean candidates, release the writer and accept a subsequent install. No-signal and committed-store semantics remain; this is not real model, .NET acquisition or publication proof. See companion-hash-cancellation-review.json.
  p2p_metadata: C58 bounds all four install metadata hash waits by the existing deadline/caller signal; late rejections are observed and no later hash, store or fetch starts. All 222 affected Node checks pass (89.57% installer line coverage), with three desktop Edge acquisition tests and final desktop/mobile hash checks passing. See p2p-metadata-cancellation-review.json; synthetic fixtures do not qualify a model or seed.
  task: C59 closes companion preparation/chunk hash cancellation gaps after C58's P2P fix; review both receipts and the full ecosystem goal before selecting the next implementation step. C57 supplies Windows/Linux packaged-consumer evidence; ARM64 and clean release admission remain open. The local API-key location and hosted-account blocker are in operations.uai; no key read or push occurred. Preserve all policy-blocked paths, including the OFb8Tf headers and their ancestors. Research stays deferred.
  maturity: Early alpha, never a working release; no code debt, obsolete code or legacy support before the owner's official acceptance of a fully working release.
  broader_goal: Ecosystem cleanup and usable release remain incomplete.
  manifest: docs/report-intake/2026-09-19/working-product-research/MANIFEST.md
  intake_verification: artifacts/ecosystem-cleanup-20260912/working-product-memory-intake-review.json
  scope: Local guidance/custody/validation only; no model run, qualification, public seed, deployment or live MemoryEndpoints operation.

current_source_state:
  cache_cleanup: Successful saved-model activation or a check with no active installation schedules one background cleanup per page, capped at sixteen passes and a 60-second cancellation signal. The chooser/chat does not await it. Issued mutations retain ownership until storage settles, with stopping/incomplete status in Advanced diagnostics and completed-pass counts. All 378 affected checks and 27 Edge tests pass. Unknown files remain; empty cleanup creates no model directories; cache/activation errors suppress cleanup.
  cache_retirement: Hash-bound orphan/superseded retirement persists and verifies a canonical staging marker outside the target directory. It survives until direct deletion, nonrecursive directory removal and observed absence. Existing pointer/staging authority remains sufficient for its own recovery path; allocation reserves the active activation ID. All 369 affected checks, nine actual Edge tests and twelve smoke observations pass. C52 now schedules startup cleanup; power-loss durability remains unproved.
  cache_startup: Read-only open and per-operation OPFS root resolution support startup's 60-second cache deadline. Late results cannot activate; timeout copy is visible in the chooser; cache/activation errors require explicit action before replacement acquisition. Verified empty caches still bootstrap automatically. All 336 affected checks, nineteen actual Edge tests and twelve direct smoke observations pass. Real-model startup timing and durable mutation/reconciliation remain open; C51 now retains terminal retirement authority.
  cache_read_cancellation: Caller signals reach file acquisition, metadata streams/hashes, enumeration, staging allocation and candidate validation. Cancelled reads do not become corruption or indeterminate-commit errors; late rejection is observed. Postcommit reconciliation drains and returns the committed candidate. C49's composition-read-cancellation-review.json retains its evidence; C50 adds startup's signal and read-only open.
  cache_readers: C48 adds shared per-composition read leases and exclusive write/retirement locks beneath the global writer lock. The app uses withRead for the full six-member worker transfer; companion validation requires that method. Scope exit/cancellation closes pending readers. Standalone member iterators pin until completion/disposal; metadata alone does not pin bytes. Real cross-tab Edge checks cover retirement and tab closure; no real model or public claim follows.
  cache_ownership: C47 requires a canonical staging marker, active pointer or hash-bound orphan manifest plus a bounded ten-file directory inventory before deletion. Unexpected entries are retained; candidate paths must be vacant. Recovery retains pointer ownership until content removal succeeds; failed candidate cleanup retains its marker. See composition-cleanup-ownership-review.json. This is synthetic storage evidence, not real model qualification or complete crash/reader lifecycle proof.
  cache_cancellation: Failed source cleanup uses the existing cancellable wait instead of an uninterruptible iterator return. The original failure and prior pointer remain authoritative; late cleanup errors are observed. Both shell hashes bind the new script. See composition-cleanup-cancellation-review.json; synthetic storage tests do not qualify a real model.
  release_smoke: Sole v8 retains raw failures and classifies only the two exact HTTP 200 probe requests after independent byte verification. Application/other failures remain blocking, with real truncation/corruption/cancellation tests. Empty startup remains deferred. C44 failures and the first failed C45 completion wait are preserved; see completed-runtime-probe-review.json. No claim that browser aborts ceased or model/deployment gates passed.
  runtime_lifetime: C43 gives runtime fetch/read/hash one 60-second default deadline and caller cancellation; admission retains 30 seconds through the shared helper. Empty startup discovers models without WASM. Exact runtime/qualification checks and activation ownership remain mandatory. See browser-runtime-lifetime-review.json; no real model, live seed or deployment.
  runtime_bytes: C42 streams manifest/WASM bytes under decoded limits before copying; 48 checks pass, including gzip/chunked HTTP and installed Edge fixtures. Two fresh builds reproduce the unchanged tracked module. Canonical scratch admits only fully contained hard-link groups. See browser-runtime-streaming-review.json; runtime wait limits and real model/public gates remain separate.
  admission_lifetime: One 30-second deadline spans both admission documents and hashes; linked caller cancellation, stream cleanup and useful timeout UI precede any model transfer. See admission-lifetime-review.json. Edge checks use synthetic metadata, with mobile viewport emulation; no real default or public seed evidence.
  task_screen: Sole planning-ledger owner is evaluator v4 with generator v2; v1-v3 evaluators, old generator and combined test retired. All 17 frozen JSON records and current tool identities unchanged; five experiments remain rejected. Twenty checks pass; see current-task-screen-review.json. No experiment replay or real model run.
  candidate_discovery: Sole owner huggingface-supported-candidates.js emits current v2 inventories for Qwen3, SmolLM2 and Qwen2.5; old Qwen-only v1 producer retired with useful tests moved. Present access flags must be false in search and revision metadata. Forty-five checks pass; see current-candidate-discovery-review.json. Metadata is not admission.
  candidate_bytes: C38 bounds decoded writes, streamed evidence and local reads; checks exact range totals and body deadlines; preserves resumable partials and removes only owned failed temporaries. Forty-nine checks pass; synthetic fixtures retired. See acquisition-byte-limits-review.json. No material/public gate passed.
  candidate_storage: C37 confines model paths to D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM and reports to canonical artifacts; rejects file links, locks each acquisition and verifies complete receipt closure against the candidate. Forty historical checks passed; see candidate-storage-review.json. C38 supplies later byte-bound corrections.
  candidate_metadata: C36 bounds original decoded JSON/text bytes, rejects oversized search rows, aborts stalled responses and preserves metadata failure codes. Native loopback HTTP proves timeout/decompression/truncation handling; no external discovery or model execution. See huggingface-metadata-review.json.
  candidate_exclusions: Current contract source-candidate-exclusions.v1.json binds 37 verified historical assessments plus the owner-rejected Qwen3 source identity. Current discovery and inventory acquisition reject known revisions and known weight-file hashes; C35's 14 historical checks are retained by useful cases in the later sole-owner suite. This is negative-only, not qualification. SmolLM2-1.7B and Qwen2.5-1.5B exact suggested revisions were already rejected; see C35/C39.
  authority: workspace.uai current_companion_truth
  implemented: Production Companion source acquisition, exclusive operation ownership, conversion, terminal reconciliation, six-member transfer/listener and browser client wiring.
  unproven: Authorized real acquisition through this coordinator, real numerical parity, useful default-model browser inference and public initial seed.
  rejected_source: Unchanged Qwen3-0.6B@c1899de289a04d12100db370d81485cdf75e47ca is diagnostic-only; identical repackaging stays rejected.
  current_numerical_contract: C30 implements v3-only registration with corrected locks/helper bindings. Historical 58 checks passed; no material v3 registration or real trace.
  environment: Canonical numerical environment admitted with synthetic framework checks; real source load and later comparison stages remain unproven.
  publication: C31 local refactor binds canonical inputs, verifies memory payloads, routes package tests through owned scratch and keeps secret-scan evidence in canonical artifacts. See publication-canonical-input-review.json for tests and limitations; transport admission still blocks live publication.
  seed_transport: C32 native server emits/exposes the descriptor-derived piece-set ID required by the browser. Actual Edge reads six synthetic member routes and rejects a foreign origin; 23 Rust, 18 companion and 48 JavaScript checks pass. See native-seed-browser-contract-review.json; no real default or live seed follows.
  static_seed_preparation: MiniModel b512402 compiles exact current descriptor bytes to six URLs, expected headers and hash-bound htaccess text. All 69 affected checks pass; no upload, local model copy, signing or catalog renewal. See MiniModel deploy/static-seed.md and its static-seed-preparation-review-20260919.json.
  static_seed_execution: MiniModel 01063a0 passes 78 affected checks including real Apache 2.4.58 GET/HEAD transfers and rejection controls with synthetic bytes. TRACE bypassed directory rules; plan now requires server/vhost TraceEnable Off. Separate WSL loopback instance and owned output removed; no TLS/browser/LiteSpeed/publication claim. See static-seed-apache-review-20260919.json and C34.

known_blockers:
  - Native internals behind complete-body abort events remain unproven; C45 reproduces them without app code and corrects the smoke evidence model. Raw events remain visible and genuine failed transfers block.
  - Source-authority scan remains incomplete on the two C28 installer links; rerun in this intake confirmed source_authority_scan_incomplete after canonical Git trust configuration.
  - Automatic approval review previously blocked C28 installer-output and other exact reviewed removals. They remain present; no alternate deletion route is authorized.
  - September 19 read-only HTTPS metadata probes see LiteSpeed, working HEAD/range/CORS and empty August 28 catalog/feed missing current authority fields. Model routes, process hosting and safe remote promotion remain unproven; this was not an independent external observer.
  - Training pilot needs genuine independent reviewers and holdout authors; no accepted derivative or 200000-record scale authorization follows from reports.

next_decisions:
  - Measure real-model startup, replacement and storage behavior under quota/device limits. C52 schedules cleanup and keeps pending mutations visible; C51 retains terminal retirement ownership, C49 cancels metadata reads and C48 protects readers. Permanently stalled mutation/commit reconciliation, power-loss behavior and complete lifecycle safety remain unproved. Do not abandon issued writes or release locks prematurely.
  - Continue historical execution-owner and producer/consumer review, independent candidate admission and remaining model/hosting work. C35-C39 provide one current discovery contract, exact exclusions, bounded transfers and complete owned receipts; tests do not grant quality/execution admission or reopen a closed experiment.
  - Test exact eligible source usefulness before conversion; diagnose semantics/arithmetic separately; measure actual browser viability.
  - Establish actual LiteSpeed hosting capabilities, server TRACE rejection, remote paths, TLS/browser CORS and qualified member readbacks. C34 proves local Apache HTTP only, using an Alias and invalid-model fixtures. MiniModel seeding is authorized; no qualified payload or deployment gate pass exists.
  - Keep restore/default under the beginner path and technical acquisition controls under Advanced; do not claim ready without the complete model.
  - Preserve frozen experiments and current six-member/Q8 contracts until evidence supports a coherent replacement.

